WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:06.880
Good morning, John, let's do a quick overview of our last day of tour just so I can remember it. Here it is.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:09.480
We've arrived at a place to stop to get food. What is it?

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:16.960
Oh, the usual. I can go to the healthy station. Yeah, you just have a single piece of cheese or...

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:21.900
What, why is that—banana milk?? Is that a real thing? Who are you signing a book for, John?

00:00:21.905 --> 00:00:23.260
- Brock's daughter.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:24.140
- Oh, that's nice.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.320
- Brock, can you be in a video?

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:27.660
- What d'you want me to do?

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.750
- Just, I'm just asking your permission to put your face in the video.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.980
- Oh, now you're gonna have to pay me a million dollars. *John laughs*

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.280
I haven't said yeah so, if I see it out there somewhere…

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.200
[Brock] - Banana milk. I wonder how they process that.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:43.752
[Hank] - Oh it smells...

00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:45.360
[Brock] - Like banana?

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.120
[Hank] - Not really. Sniff it. What do you think?

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:48.200
[John] - Did you really say that?

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:49.840
[Brock] - It smells like that, uh, candy.

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:55.409
[John] - Oh yeah, banana 'now &amp; laters'. Oh. Oh god. That's, that smells awful. That smells like fake bananas.

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:57.410
[Hank] - It was in the healthy section

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.400
[Hank] - And now we stop for

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:15.660
video making for John's video. Pet area. Does that dog have a crown on it? It's a king dog. His name is Crown.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:18.540
He's got a poop. John found a real weird tree.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.879
[John] - Weird tree! It like doesn't have a trunk,

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.960
It's like a tree made out of dirt!

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:23.960
[Hank] - Ooh, nice chain, John.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.240
Careful, though, don't hurt yourself.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:27.860
[John] - Thank you.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:32.360
[Hank] - I mean, Pizza John photoshoot time, look at this chain. Oh, yeah.

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:35.530
Your chain's real dirty.

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:37.400
[John] - I actually don't want this on my body anymore.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:39.440
[Hank] - Oh, can we actually go into the farm?

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.040
[John] - Heck yeah we can.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:41.820
[Hank] - It's unlocked.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:43.024
[John] - I mean, that actually is a beautiful...

00:01:43.024 --> 00:01:44.000
[Hank] - It's super cool

00:01:44.380 --> 00:02:16.340
*cool guy music*

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:18.540
- You ready, John?

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:19.960
- I'm ready, let's do it.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:20.960
- Last show.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:22.120
- Aren't you gonna miss the bus so much?

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:25.640
- Hello! Thanks for showing up real early.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:33.239
Thanks. Oh my god, this is a big place. Hey, there it is, in the basement. These are the books John's gonna sign.

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:52.100
- How you feelin'?

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.700
- Good. A little nervous, I'm just going through our questions.

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:55.420
- Oh, we got questions.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:56.318
- We got questions.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:59.160
- And we got donuts!

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:01.800
That doesn't happen every night. Thank you to whoever gave us donuts.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.960
[John] - I would now like to bring to the stage for the very first time *laughter*

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:08.100
*laughter* my brother Hank.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:15.220
Human brains are remarkably flexible. I've been lucky enough to have had a bunch of moments of tremendous

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:21.920
sositive shift in my life going to college, to summer camp, moving to a new place, going on and coming back from tour.

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:27.990
It's amazing how fast I find my brain shifts to accept that this new life is my life now.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:33.800
And then when I go back to my old life, that life is my life now. That transition is overwhelming, yeah, definitely,

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:38.980
but it also, it's an opportunity to examine my work and what I want to be doing

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:42.480
and I'm very glad to have shared this intense experience with you, John, and with

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:48.989
so many other people and to have made people happy and to just think out loud about what it means to be a person.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:54.480
But I am also very very very happy to be back home. John, I'll see you on Tuesday

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:57.640
This doesn't feel weird in a pecan orchard at all. People are watching me

